Organization = {ISHS, Div Hort Human Hlth; ISHS, Working Grp Hort Therapy},
Abstract = {This study explores the physiological and psychological impacts of the
   field and non-field leisure farm landscapes on human beings. The leisure
   farm landscapes in this study are divided into garden, waterscape, and
   tunnel trellis. In terms of the psychological part, two psychological
   questionnaires: attention restoration and preference level are used for
   the measurement, while physiological feedback instruments are used to
   measure three physiological indicators: EMG, EEG, and heart rate. The
   qualities of being away, fascination, and preference level in attention
   restoration have no significant difference with EMG and EEG. In terms of
   the heart rate, it is higher in non-field when viewing the garden
   landscape, possibly because of the influence of the surrounding parrot
   noises. Except for the visual perception in the field testing, the other
   senses are also influenced. The exploration of the visual benefits in
   the non-field testing is beneficial for the test variable control
   management.},
