   MALAYSIA, DEC 06-08, 2016},
Organization = {Wessex Inst; Univ Teknologi Mara; Univ Sains Malaysia; WIT Transact Ecol
   \& Environm; Int Journal Sustainable Dev \& Planning},
Abstract = {The Vendee Globe is becoming a mythical event for Sables d'Olonne. It is
   the ``Vendee Blue Gold!{''}, which is how we know it today. In 2014, the
   Vendee Globe was considered a fascinating event, self-made by the area,
   so it may be considered as Vendean Heritage, well identified and
   developed by all the inhabitants who are able to participate and
   collaborate in its success. They are really proud of it. It is an
   excellent example of a sustainable tourism project and a successful
   event created by local people. Vendee Globe is today a landmark.
   How has this famous event galvanized and is continuing to galvanize
   people for action towards sustainable development of the city and its
   surrounding region? It has generated a real urban and country
   metamorphosis and a new local dynamic since 1989 and has changed
   attitudes.
   To study this evolution, the common methods and participative techniques
   that have been used or are still used across both categories:
   interviews: individual and in depth (100/year ante and post and during
   the event), focus groups with stakeholders and partners took place
   during each phase and episode of Vendee Globe. Elements as indicators
   have been chosen and analyzed after every race to try to estimate
   internal and external effects on the territory and landing management.
   But will the management of the race escape from its local partners in
   the future?},
