Organization = {Singapore Management \& Sports Sci Inst; Acad Conf Inst},
Abstract = {The characteristics of Chu people in their color aesthetic include
   respecting red and pay attention to its contrast with black, skilled use
   of blended colors. When they are influenced by Confucian concept of
   color, Chu people seek for beautiful, romantic, mysterious color. There
   are reasons about Chu people's color psychology. The natural environment
   and witchcraft sorcery customs, Chu people's time and space perception
   and ancestral consciousness are main factors of the formation of their
   color aesthetic psychology.
   Chu's color aesthetic formed in the era of Central Plains Confucian
   aesthetic fashion. It is influenced by Confucian concept of color, but
   the aesthetic psychology of Chu people is different from the former,
   which exhibits a gorgeous, heavy and complicated, gorgeous romantic
   character. This paper focuses on the aesthetic characteristics of color
   and their psychological causes, combined with the history, art,
   folklore, psychology research methods.},
