   Law; Univ Negeri Surabaya, Fac Math \& Nat Sci; Univ Trunojoyo Madura,
   Fac Engn},
Abstract = {Organizational culture is a fundamental basis for an organization. The
   meaning of organizational culture in the lives of all the perceptions
   and attitudes that arise from the interaction of a person with a job,
   others, and the environment. The purpose of this study was to determine
   how much the role of organizational culture on the performance of
   primary school teachers. To solve these problems we used survey approach
   with multiple correlations. This approach is used to explain the role of
   organizational culture on the performance of elementary school teachers.
   The results using these approaches suggests that the role of
   organizational culture on performance of primary school teachers who
   described the path coefficient of 0.066899, the value of t statistic of
   0.903617 below +/- 1.654, it means that organizational culture has a
   positive role albeit indirectly against elementary school teacher's
   performance is made possible through job satisfaction.},
