Note = {24th International Symposium on Research and Applications in Psychology
   (SICAP) - Cognitive Characteristics of Transdisciplinarity. Applications
   in Psychology and Psychotherapies, Timisoara, ROMANIA, MAR 24-26, 2017},
Abstract = {This study is a part of a larger research on the improvement of several
   cognitive abilities of primary school children using mind stimulating
   games. One of these games used as stimulation for cognitive skills was
   Tangram, which is a well-known game around the world and has long been
   recognized as a mind stimulating game. The objective of the study was to
   illustrate the influence of regular Tangram playing sessions upon
   several cognitive abilities: attention stability, attention
   concentration capacity, visual memory, analytical reasoning, analogical
   transfer, categorization flexibility, spatial orientation,
   transformation of mental images, visual perception. The data processed
   was collected over a period of three years from 26 children, aged
   between 6-10 years old, with whom individual play sessions were
   organized twice a week for a period of three months. The final test
   results show great improvement in many areas compared with the
   pretesting data.},
