Note = {2024 International Conference on Energy and Environment-ICEE-Bringing
   together Engineering and Economics, Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, JUN 06-07, 2024},
Abstract = {The article examines the social, environmental and economic impacts of
   the Belo Monte Hydroelectric Plant, located in the state of Para,
   Brazil, one of the largest projects of its type in the world. While
   hydropower generation is generally considered clean, in environmental
   terms, this study highlights the complex interactions involved in
   analyzing stakeholder perceptions. The stakeholders considered and
   interviewed are local residents, members of Non-Governmental
   Organizations and social movements, experts, journalists, members of the
   business community and institutional representatives. The dimensions
   analysed were environmental and social impacts, regional economic
   consequences, actions to minimize adverse impacts and strengthen
   positive aspects. In particular, effects such as reduced fishing,
   changes in social dynamics and increased violence, as well as benefits
   such as job creation and strengthening the regional economy were found.
   The analysis contributes to a more comprehensive understanding of the
   true impacts and benefits associated with large-scale hydropower
   projects.},
