   Mediterranean Area, Vols 1 and 2},
Year = {2006},
Pages = {365-370},
Note = {1st International Symposium on Environment Identities and Mediterranean
   Area, Corte Ajaccio, FRANCE, JUL 10-13, 2006},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {Tommaseo left Florence to go into exile in France, from 1834 to 1838. In
   order to discover what this stay brougt to him, we should to examine
   what the writer successively felt in Paris, in Nantes, then in Corsica,
   his perception of the cities and the areas which he visited, but also
   his frequentations and and his activities. More than just allowing us to
   discover his french experience, the study of his private writings
   reveals that Tommaseo carries out himself an assessment of this period
   in his novel Fede e bellezza. Indeed, in this novel which presents an
   autobiographical dimension, we discover what he felt and learned, during
   his stay in France. Thus, we noticed that his exile influenced his
   novel, of which representations of Paris and Corsica in particular
   reveal the feelings and the ideological convictions of the writer, as
   much as his aspirations for Italy.},
