   Construct \& Building Phys; Tech Chamber Greece},
Abstract = {This study examines - by means of numerical analysis - the thermal,
   environmental and structural performance of an innovative modular
   masonry system that is currently under development. Focus is given on
   investigating the response of the system when alternative geometries of
   brick units are used and different insulation materials are incorporated
   into the core of the masonry. Heat flux analysis is performed to examine
   temperature distribution within the structure and to estimate its
   U-value. The embodied energy of the assemblage is computed and compared
   against commonly used masonry systems. Furthermore, non-linear Finite
   Element (FE) simulation is conducted to assess load resistance. Results
   indicate that the proposed solution has the potential to produce energy
   efficient and structurally sound constructions. (C) 2017 The Authors.
