   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc},
Abstract = {Modern society is not sustainable without the contributions of
   engineers. In order for engineers to use their skills and knowledge most
   effectively for the upholding of sustainable development principles,
   they need to be properly educated in disciplines pertaining to
   infrastructure, environment and energy. This paper describes a new
   course which has been developed at The University of Hong Kong entitled
   Engineering for Sustainable Development. The course provides an
   introduction to first year undergraduate engineering students to the
   fields of civil, environmental and mechanical engineering in the context
   of sustainable development while adopting an outcome based learning
   approach. A detailed account of the contents of the course is provided
   in this paper comprising of, but not limited to, course aims, learning
   outcomes, individual lecture contents as well as assessment tasks. The
   alignments between the various components of the course are also
   provided in addition to evolution of the course in light of student
   feedback.},
