Organization = {Int Journal Appl Energy; Appl Energy Innovat Inst; China Assoc Sci \&
   Technol HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile},
Abstract = {The present study analyzed both production-based and consumption-based
   carbon emissions of Beijing. Based on the detailed carbon emission
   inventory, the input-output analysis was applied to calculate the
   consumption-based carbon emissions of the local economic system. Due to
   the constraint of input-output data, the CO2 emissions originated from
   fossil fuel combustion in 2002, 2005, 2007, 2010 and 2012 were studied.
   According to the results, Beijing's production-based carbon emissions
   may have reached the peak before 2010. More and more carbon emissions
   were embodied in Beijing's domestic exports. While even more local
   carbon emission were avoided by Beijing's domestic and foreign imports.
