   Technol; Anhui Environm Sci Soc},
Abstract = {A bioflocculant-producing bacterium isolated from activated sludge,
   named B3, was identified as Klebsiella sp. by biomicroscope
   morphological observation, 16S rDNA sequence identification and
   physiological and biochemical characteristics. The bioflocculant.
   produced by B3 was named MBFB3. The most favorable medium component for
   bioflocculants producing were sucrose 16g/L, (NH4)(2)SO4 lg/L, K2-Mat
   lg/L and initial pH about 8.0, respectively. The study of growth curve
   indicated the flocculating activity of MBFB3 could reach 96.65\% on the
   optimum condition after 6h, which was greatly shorter than all the other
   reported strains required. In order to reduce the costs of MBFB3, the
   strain was cultured in various organic wastewaters from food production.
   The results indicated that strain B3 could rapidly grow and synthesize
   plenty of extra cellular flocculants under the condition of the
   approximately diluted brewery wastewater, dairy wastewater and flourmill
   wastewater without addition carbon and nitrogen source.},
