   Div Water Sci; WHO UNEP Global Environm Monitoring Syst; Severn Trent
   Water; Entec Europe Ltd; NIREX UK Ltd; Environm Agcy},
Abstract = {Pollution from road drainage is a potential source of groundwater
   contamination but fluxes to soakaways, and the chemical nature and
   concentrations of contaminants are largely unknown. Pollutants may arise
   from diffuse sources such as fuel additives deposited to the road
   surface, or from point sources such as accidental spillages. A
   comprehensive and balanced evaluation of the threat to groundwater
   quality is needed to aid improvements in the protection of groundwater;
   for example, improving policy formulation and the design and placement
   of highway drainage. This paper reviews work on potential
   highway-derived pollutants and explains the need for the development of
   a risk assessment methodology which is widely accepted by interested
   parties in the UK.},
