   AGRICULTURE IN THE TROPICS (IC-FSSAT)},
Series = {IOP Conference Series-Earth and Environmental Science},
Year = {2018},
Volume = {157},
Note = {1st International Conference on Food Security and Sustainable
   Agriculture in The Tropics (IC-FSSAT), Hasanuddin Univ, Fac Agr \&
   Publicat Management Ctr, Makassar, INDONESIA, OCT 24-25, 2017},
Abstract = {Otak-otak is one indigenous foods from Indonesia which made from fish
   paste, tapioca flour and spices. The aim of this research was to produce
   premix flour for making otak-otak using mackerel surimi, tapioca flour
   and spices and to evaluate their chemical properties and sensory
   acceptability of the product. Mackerel surimi was first dried, miled
   into powder form then mixed with tapioca flour and spices. The result
   showed that, otak-otak which made from Premix-B formula (40\% mackerel
   surimi powder and 60\% tapioca flour) was the best result for all
   sensory attributes. It presented ``like moderately{''} for hedonic
   score. Protein, ash, moisture, carbohydrate, and fat contents of the
   premix-B formula were 23.51\%, 2.44\%, 7.31\%, 71.02\%, 4.28\%,
   respectively, which met the SNI requirements. Overall, this study
   clearly showed that it was possible to make otak-otak with less
   complicated process and the product did not have any negative results on
   sensory perception.},
