   Univ, Nanchang, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 23-25, 2010},
Organization = {Pan Asian Soc Sports \& Phys Educ},
Abstract = {The purpose of this study was to examine the relationship between
   physical self-concept and physical activity based on method of
   meta-analysis Total 52 research reports were collected to meet the
   requirements of the study, with a sample size of 3520 individuals The
   results indicated that (a) the effect size was an interval of between 0
   28 and 0 60, which was a medium effect, (b) the scores of 5 sub-scale of
   Physical Self-Perception Profile (PSPP) was not equal exactly, such as
   perceived sport competence was best and body attractiveness was worst
   (c) high physical activity intensity was more effective than low on
   physical self-concept, and (d) the effects was influenced by gender,
   sports events and so on It can been concluded that regular physical
   activity was a factor of enhancing physical self-concept, further study
   must be done on more widely range of samples such as non-school student
   groups or non-regular physical activity people groups},
